  "body": "## Problem\nThe market observer already opens every unresolved Vinted listing sequentially, but some item pages still remained unresolved. Runtime showed 49/70 timestamps resolved on one catalog page even though all 70 detail pages were opened.\n\nDevTools confirmed the live Vinted DOM uses an exact field:\n\n`[data-testid=\"item-attributes-upload_date\"] [itemprop=\"upload_date\"]`\n\nand for the one-week singular case Vinted can render the value literally as `tygodnia`, with no numeric prefix and no `datetime` attribute. The old generic `Dodane` text scan rejected that value.\n\n## Changes\n- Read the confirmed `item-attributes-upload_date` field first, before generic text/JSON-LD/hydrated fallbacks.\n- Use `[itemprop=\"upload_date\"]` as the value source and preserve a `datetime` value if Vinted provides one.\n- Parse the confirmed singular `tygodnia` label as one week before the observation time.\n- Keep the existing sequential detail-page navigation, 1.5 s pacing, 403/429 backoff, session-refresh handling, catalog restore and metadata fallbacks unchanged.\n- Add regression tests for the exact selector and singular week label.\n\n## Calendar semantics\nNo backend calendar change is needed. Existing planning already uses Europe/Warsaw, local midnight for Today, Monday 00:00 for the current week, and the preceding Monday-to-Monday interval for the previous full week.\n\n## Scope\n- Market statistics publication-time resolver only.\n- No normal bot scheduling, negotiation, session, mobile or frontend behavior changes.\n\n## Tests\n- Playwright unit tests / full repository CI.",
